  "response": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>March Filing Fee Retention</title>\n<style>\n  :root{\n    --ink:#1d2430; --muted:#5b6777; --line:#dfe4ec;\n    --accent:#2f5d94; --accent-soft:#eaf1fa; --warn:#8a5a00; --warn-soft:#fff5e0;\n  }\n  *{box-sizing:border-box}\n  body{\n    margin:0; padding:2.5rem 1.25rem 4rem;\n    font:16px/1.6 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\n    color:var(--ink); background:#f6f8fb;\n  }\n  main{max-width:820px; margin:0 auto}\n  h1{font-size:1.6rem; margin:0 0 .25rem}\n  .sub{color:var(--muted); margin:0 0 2rem}\n  section{background:#fff; border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:10px; padding:1.25rem 1.5rem; margin-bottom:1.25rem}\n  h2{font-size:1.05rem; margin:0 0 .75rem; color:var(--accent); letter-spacing:.02em; text-transform:uppercase}\n  table{width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; margin:.5rem 0}\n  th,td{padding:.5rem .6rem; text-align:right; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}\n  th:first-child,td:first-child{text-align:left}\n  th{font-size:.82rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.04em; color:var(--muted)}\n  tfoot td{font-weight:700; border-bottom:none; border-top:2px solid var(--ink)}\n  .answer{background:var(--accent-soft); border:1px solid var(--accent); border-radius:10px;\n    padding:1.25rem 1.5rem; margin-bottom:1.5rem}\n  .answer .label{font-size:.82rem; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.06em; color:var(--accent)}\n  .answer .value{font-size:2.4rem; font-weight:700; line-height:1.2}\n  .note{background:var(--warn-soft); border-left:4px solid var(--warn); padding:.75rem 1rem; border-radius:4px; color:#4a3500}\n  code{background:#f0f3f8; padding:.1rem .35rem; border-radius:4px; font-size:.92em}\n  ul{margin:.25rem 0 .5rem; padding-left:1.2rem}\n  .step{margin-bottom:1.1rem}\n  .step:last-child{margin-bottom:0}\n  .step .calc{font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:.93rem; background:#f0f3f8;\n    padding:.5rem .7rem; border-radius:6px; display:block; margin-top:.35rem; overflow-x:auto}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<main>\n\n  <h1>Regional Courthouse \u2014 March Filing Fees</h1>\n  <p class=\"sub\">How much did the courthouse <strong>retain</strong> from filing fees collected in March?</p>\n\n  <div class=\"answer\">\n    <div class=\"label\">Answer</div>\n    <div class=\"value\">$58,682</div>\n    <div>82% of $71,563 in net filing-fee collections (exact: $58,681.66).</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <section>\n    <h2>The problem</h2>\n    <ul>\n      <li>420 civil filings @ $85 \u00b7 175 family-law filings @ $120 \u00b7 60 probate filings @ $210</li>\n      <li>6% state surcharge added to every filing fee</li>\n      <li>$5 e-filing credit per electronic filing \u2014 70% civil, 40% family, 25% probate</li>\n      <li>Courthouse retains 82%; 18% remitted to the state</li>\n      <li>Passport desk took in $9,400 \u2014 handled separately</li>\n    </ul>\n  </section>\n\n  <section>\n    <h2>Step 1 \u2014 Base fees by case type</h2>\n    <table>\n      <thead>\n        <tr><th>Case type</th><th>Filings</th><th>Base fee</th><th>Base total</th></tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td>Civil</td><td>420</td><td>$85</td><td>$35,700</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Family law</td><td>175</td><td>$120</td><td>$21,000</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Probate</td><td>60</td><td>$210</td><td>$12,600</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n      <tfoot>\n        <tr><td>Total</td><td>655</td><td></td><td>$69,300</td></tr>\n      </tfoot>\n    </table>\n  </section>\n\n  <section>\n    <h2>Step 2 \u2014 Add the 6% state surcharge</h2>\n    <div class=\"step\">\n      The surcharge applies to every filing fee, so it scales the whole base total.\n      <span class=\"calc\">$69,300 \u00d7 1.06 = $73,458.00</span>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <section>\n    <h2>Step 3 \u2014 Subtract e-filing credits</h2>\n    <p>The $5 credit is a flat per-filing deduction, so count the electronic filings.</p>\n    <table>\n      <thead>\n        <tr><th>Case type</th><th>Filings</th><th>% electronic</th><th>E-filings</th><th>Credit</th></tr>\n      </thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td>Civil</td><td>420</td><td>70%</td><td>294</td><td>$1,470</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Family law</td><td>175</td><td>40%</td><td>70</td><td>$350</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Probate</td><td>60</td><td>25%</td><td>15</td><td>$75</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n      <tfoot>\n        <tr><td>Total</td><td>655</td><td></td><td>379</td><td>$1,895</td></tr>\n      </tfoot>\n    </table>\n    <div class=\"step\">\n      <span class=\"calc\">$73,458.00 \u2212 $1,895.00 = $71,563.00 collected</span>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <section>\n    <h2>Step 4 \u2014 Apply the 82% retention split</h2>\n    <div class=\"step\">\n      <span class=\"calc\">$71,563.00 \u00d7 0.82 = $58,681.66  \u2192  $58,682</span>\n      Remitted to the state: $71,563.00 \u00d7 0.18 = $12,881.34. The two parts sum back to $71,563.00. \u2713\n    </div>\n  </section>\n\n  <section>\n    <h2>Traps avoided</h2>\n    <div class=\"note\">\n      <strong>Passport revenue is excluded.</strong> The $9,400 is explicitly not part of filing fee\n      collections, so it never enters the calculation \u2014 including it would wrongly give\n      <code>$80,963 \u00d7 0.82 = $66,390</code>.\n    </div>\n    <p style=\"margin-top:.9rem\">Two other easy slips: the surcharge applies <em>before</em> the flat $5 credit\n    (a credit is deducted from what the filer owes, it is not itself surcharged), and the $5 credit is a flat\n    amount per filing rather than a percentage \u2014 so it depends on the <em>count</em> of e-filings (379), not on fee size.</p>\n  </section>\n\n</main>\n</body>\n</html>",
